    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0317" n="215" xml:id="pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5936: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-28T10:00:00+08:00">February 28, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 28—2:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>191. My 172, February 21, 3 p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d204-f1"/> Drysdale<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d204-f2"/> returned last night reports forces of Tang Yu-lin
                    as retreating from Chaoyang in a westerly direction towards Chihfeng leaving
                    forces of Chang Hseuh-liang to meet Japanese main thrust Chaoyang, Lingyuan,
                    Pingchwan, Chengteh. Chinese first line of resistance at Lingyuan. Chinese plan
                    contemplates Japanese advance Shanhaikwan, Lulung, Fengjun, Yiitien, Sanho,
                    Tungchow-Peiping Road, aimed at cutting off Peiping-Jehol communications. It is
                    not expected that Japanese thrust inside Wall will occur unless Japanese thrust
                    from Chaoyang is held up. Drysdale reports civilian population as far as
                    Lingyuan and beyond calm while Chinese forces moving forward to positions with
                    determination and desire to fight. Chief weakness Chinese forces lies in supply
                    and leadership. Chinese now concentrating with the assistance of Nanking on
                    problem of supply.</p>
                <p>By mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <p>Please inform War Department confidentially.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
